teo. |\n\nThings to check before this goes to Mateo:\n- **#8841 history doesn't line up.**\n  - The 4/27 digest puts it at Allentown, 5/4 has it open, and 7/1 has it closed.\n  - The 9/30 digest has it submitted and escalated again, this time at \"Newark\", which the 4/27 digest ties to the Mobility depot.\n  - It may be a reopen, a reused number, or a digest error. I can't tell from what I can see.\n- **The #PD- prefix** appears only in the 4/27 digest. Everywhere else it is plain #8841.\n- **No ticket numbers appear in** Moss's 3/10/2025, 7/7/2025, 12/1/2025, 5/3/2026, 8/3/2026 digests or the cheat sheet. Those mention Vantorre Group issues (gate delays, Door 14 duplicate entries, Mateo's export question) without a number. The 3/10/2025 and 5/3/2026 digests refer to emails or an \"existing support thread\".\n\nI can only see these three sources, so this is not a full ticket history from the support system. Gideon, who now owns the account, or support could confirm the exact #8841 timeline."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"C36LMHRLAXI","ts":"1792159200.000126"}}
